A thread that becomes ready joins a queue of the core that settles it rather than of the core it runs on,
so a signal from another core puts the thread where its units are not; each core's queues hold its own threads.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a core's queue holds a place of another core
Report: the kernel reached outside RAM

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -342,7 +342,7 @@ static void place_settle(struct place *p)
         }
         p->core = (uint8_t)(core - cores);
         if (queue != QUEUE_NONE) {
-            ring_push(queue_head(core, queue), v2p(p), QUEUED);
+            ring_push(queue_head(core_self(), queue), v2p(p), QUEUED);
         }
         p->queue = queue;
     }
